ully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"ZInQ.FrozenTarget","summary":"There is a polynomial $P\\in\\mathbb Z[X_0,\\ldots,X_{292890231904}]$ of total degree less than $2\\uparrow\\uparrow 7$, every coefficient of which has absolute value less than $2\\uparrow\\uparrow 8$, such that for every $q\\in\\mathbb Q$,","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#frozen-target"},{"id":"main/six-contact-estimate","title":"The six-contact height estimate","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"ZInQ.SixContactEstimate","summary":"Let $\\mathcal C=\\{0,-15,-20,-24,-30,-60\\}$. For a finite set $S$ of primes containing every prime at most $324$ and $u\\in\\mathbb Q\\setminus\\mathcal C$, let $M_S(u)$ be the product of the primes $p\\notin S$ for which $v_p(u-c)$ is positive and odd for some $c\\in\\mathcal C$. Put $F_0=324!$, $D=F_0\\,3^{256F_0^4}$, $G_0=116064000000$, $E_0=10(DG_0)^2$, $Q_R=R^{RE_0}$, $B_{\\rm cm}=D^2\\,3^{21000D^2}+1$,…","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#six-contact-estimate"},{"id":"main/six-contact-min","title":"The minimal height hypothesis","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"ZInQ.SixContactMin","summary":"Let $\\mathcal C$, $h$, $M_S$, $D$, $E_0$ and $C_{\\rm cm}$ be as in the six-contact height estimate, and put Let $S_{\\rm mul}=S_{\\rm ht}\\cup\\mathcal H\\cup\\{p\\text{ prime}:p\\mid c_*\\}$ be the prime set of the multiplication certificate: $S_{\\rm ht}$ is the set of primes at most $324$, $\\mathcal H$ is the prime catalogue (the first twenty-two primes greater than $324$ in each unit class modulo $W=4P_s$), and…","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#six-contact-min"},{"id":"main/six-contact-min-of-estimate","title":"The six-contact estimate implies its minimal form","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.sixContactMin_of_sixContactEstimate, ZInQ.Mult.le_heightD_of_mem_S_mul","summary":"Every prime of $S_{\\rm mul}$ is at most $D$. Consequently the six-contact height estimate implies the minimal height hypothesis: for every $u\\in\\mathbb Q\\setminus\\mathcal C$, $h(u)\\le H_6(D)\\,M_{S_{\\rm mul}}(u)^{24}$.","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#six-contact-min-of-estimate"},{"id":"main/pole-completeness","title":"Pole completeness","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"ZInQ.PoleCompleteness, ZInQ.polePoly, ZInQ.PoleSoluble, ZInQ.poleS0","summary":"For $B\\in\\mathbb Q$ and witnesses $b_0,\\ldots,b_5,e,z,r_1,r_2,w\\in\\mathbb Q$ put $m=(1-2b_0)(1+b_1)(1+2b_2)(1+4b_3)(1+6b_4)(1+12b_5)$, $A=mB$, $H=A(A-B^2)$, $T_1=A(A-e)(A+e)$, $T_2=A(Az^2-eH)(Az^2+eH)$ and Write $\\Phi(B)$ when $Q_{\\rm pole}$ has a rational zero with input $B$. For $B\\ne0$ a zero puts $(A,r_1)$ on the congruent number curve $y^2=x(x-e)(x+e)$ and $(Az^2,zr_2)$ on $y^2=x(x-eH)(x+eH)$.","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#pole-completeness"},{"id":"main/certified-rank","title":"The certified rank hypothesis","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"ZInQ.CertifiedRank","summary":"For an integer $d$ let $C_d$ be the congruent number curve $y^2=x^3-d^2x$. The certified rank hypothesis CR₃ is the following assertion. Let $d$ be a squarefree positive integer with $d\\equiv5\\pmod8$, and let $a$ be a squarefree integer dividing $d$ with $|a|\\equiv7\\pmod8$. Suppose that the Selmer system $\\Sigma(\\mathcal C_d)$ of the configuration of $d$ has exactly $8$ solutions and that one of them has first…","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#certified-rank"},{"id":"main/mordell-weil","title":"Mordell–Weil for the generator curve","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"ZInQ.MordellWeilE","summary":"The group $E(K_0)$ of $K_0$-rational points of $E:y^2=x^3-d^2x$, with $K_0=\\mathbb Q(\\sqrt2)$ and $d=75-53\\sqrt2$, is finitely generated.","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#mordell-weil"},{"id":"main/prime-pattern","title":"The twenty-two-prime pattern","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"ZInQ.FixedPrimePattern","summary":"Let $P_s$ be the product of the primes at most $324$ and $W=4P_s$. Let $\\mathcal H$ consist of the first twenty-two primes greater than $324$ in each unit residue class modulo $W$, and $\\mathcal K=\\{dh: d\\mid P_s^4,\\ d>0,\\ h\\in\\mathcal H\\}$. Call a prime $p$ good if it splits in $\\mathbb Q(\\sqrt2)$, both reductions of $E$ at the places above $p$ are good, and their orders $d_1,d_2$ satisfy $\\gcd(d_1,d_2)=4$ and…","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#prime-pattern"},{"id":"main/catalogue-bound","title":"The catalogue bound","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"ZInQ.CatalogueBound8, ZInQ.CatalogueBound","summary":"With $W=4P_s$ as in the prime pattern, every unit residue class modulo $W$ contains at least twenty-two primes $p$ with $324<p<2^{W^8}$.","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#catalogue-bound"},{"id":"main/two-slope-pattern","title":"The two-slope prime pattern","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Definition","lean":"ZInQ.TwoSlopePattern, ZInQ.GoodSlopePrime","summary":"Let $\\mathcal C=\\{0,-15,-20,-24,-30,-60\\}$, let $\\mathcal H$ be the prime catalogue of the twenty-two-prime pattern (the first twenty-two primes greater than $324$ in each unit residue class modulo $W=4P_s$), and $E:y^2=x^3-(75-53\\sqrt2)^2x$. Call a prime $p$ a *good slope prime* if there is $r\\in\\mathbb Z/p$ with $r^2=2$, $75-53r\\ne0$ and $75+53r\\ne0$ in $\\mathbb Z/p$, and the numbers $d_1,d_2$ of points, the…","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#two-slope-pattern"},{"id":"main/main-theorem","title":"The main theorem","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactEstimate, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_addMulBound, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_twoSlopePattern, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_poleCompleteness, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_nodeCheck","summary":"Assume the minimal height hypothesis, the certified rank hypothesis CR₃ and the twenty-two-prime pattern. Then the target statement holds: some integer polynomial in $292{,}890{,}231{,}905$ variables, of degree below $2\\uparrow\\uparrow7$ and with coefficients below $2\\uparrow\\uparrow8$, has rational zero projection to its first variable exactly $\\mathbb Z$.","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#main-theorem"},{"id":"main/main-theorem-two-hypotheses","title":"The main theorem from two hypotheses","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRank, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_goodPrimeDensity, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_greenTaoDense, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_goodPrimeAP","summary":"Assume the minimal height hypothesis and the certified rank hypothesis CR₃. Then the target statement holds: some integer polynomial in $292{,}890{,}231{,}905$ variables, of degree below $2\\uparrow\\uparrow7$ and with coefficients below $2\\uparrow\\uparrow8$, has rational zero projection to its first variable exactly $\\mathbb Z$.","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#main-theorem-two-hypotheses"},{"id":"main/main-theorem-selmer","title":"The main theorem from the Selmer form of the rank hypothesis","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankSel, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRank5b, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_certifiedRankSel_goodPrimeDensity, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_certifiedRankSel_greenTaoDense, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_certifiedRankSel, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_certifiedRank5b","summary":"Assume the minimal height hypothesis and the Selmer form CR₃^Sel of the certified rank hypothesis. Then the target statement holds, for the same polynomial as in the main theorem.","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#main-theorem-selmer"},{"id":"main/main-theorem-tyz","title":"The main theorem from the Tian–Yuan–Zhang forms of the rank hypothesis","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankTYZ, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankTYZCl","summary":"Assume the minimal height hypothesis and the Tian–Yuan–Zhang form CR₃^TYZ of the certified rank hypothesis. Then the target statement holds, for the same polynomial as in the main theorem. The theorem also holds under the minimal height hypothesis and the class-number form CR₃^TYZ_Cl.","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#main-theorem-tyz"},{"id":"main/main-theorem-positive-rank","title":"The main theorem from the positive-rank forms of the rank hypothesis","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankRk, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankTYZRk, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankTYZClRk","summary":"Assume the minimal height hypothesis and the positive-rank form CR₃^Rk of the certified rank hypothesis. Then the target statement holds, for the same polynomial as in the main theorem. The theorem also holds under the minimal height hypothesis and CR₃^TYZ,Rk, and under the minimal height hypothesis and CR₃^TYZ_Cl,Rk.","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#main-theorem-positive-rank"},{"id":"main/main-theorem-two-curves","title":"The main theorem from positive rank on the two curves of a slot choice","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankDLRk, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankDLAdmRk","summary":"Assume the minimal height hypothesis and the hypothesis CR₃^DL,Rk. Then the target statement holds, for the same polynomial as in the main theorem.","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#main-theorem-two-curves"},{"id":"main/main-theorem-infinitely-many-points","title":"The main theorem from the infinitely-many-points forms of the rank hypothesis","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankInf, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankTYZInf, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankTYZClInf, ZInQ.exists_bounded_integer_polynomial_defining_integers_of_sixContactMin_certifiedRankDLInf","summary":"Assume the minimal height hypothesis and the hypothesis CR₃^Inf. Then the target statement holds, as in the main theorem. The theorem also holds under the minimal height hypothesis and CR₃^TYZ,Inf, under the minimal height hypothesis and CR₃^TYZ_Cl,Inf, and under the minimal height hypothesis and CR₃^DL,Inf.","route":"../roadmap/main/index.html#main-theorem-infinitely-many-points"}],"result_edges":[["main/main-theorem","main/certified-rank",1,0],["main/main-theorem-two-hypotheses","main/certified-rank",1,0],["main/main-theorem","main/frozen-target",1,0],["main/main-theorem-infinitely-many-points","main/frozen-target",1,0],["main/main-theorem-positive-rank","main/frozen-target",1,0],["main/main-theorem-selmer","main/frozen-target",1,0],["main/main-theorem-two-curves","main/frozen-target",1,0],["main/main-theorem-two-hypotheses","main/frozen-target",1,0],["main/main-theorem-tyz","main/frozen-target",1,0],["main/main-theorem-selmer","main/main-theorem",0,1],["main/main-theorem-two-hypotheses","main/main-theorem",0,1],["main/main-t